# Ornith 1.0 35B on a 24 GB card
#
# Restore with:
#     cp docs/profiles/ornith-35b.env .env
#     $EDITOR .env                          # MODELS_DIR is machine-specific
#     ./scripts/serve.sh up
#
# This is the deployment serving the model on an RTX 4090 — the exact config
# that won the A/B test in EXPERIMENTS.md section 10, no corrections applied.
# CACHE_RAM is the one addition: it is carried over from the 3090 work
# (EXPERIMENTS.md section 3) and, as of writing, not re-measured on the 4090.
# docs/models.md section 3, EXPERIMENTS.md section 10.

# --- Where the .gguf files live on the host ---
MODELS_DIR=/home/nromero/models

# --- Model ---
# unsloth/Ornith-1.0-35B-GGUF — 22.3 GB, MIT licensed.
MODEL_FILE=Ornith-1.0-35B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf
MODEL_ALIAS=ornith-35b
CONTAINER_NAME=ornith
PORT=8080

# --- Memory ---
# 131072 is affordable here even though the model is larger than Qwen3.8-27B,
# because its KV cache is far cheaper: head_count_kv is 2 rather than 4, and 10
# of its 40 blocks carry KV rather than 17 of 65. That is 10.6 KiB/token at
# q8_0 — 1,360 MiB at this context, against Qwen's 2,312 MiB at half of it.
# 22.3 GB of weights plus that cache measured 23,117 of 24,564 MiB in use.
# It fits, but with under 1.5 GB of margin: do not raise CTX further.
# KV_TYPE=q4_0 is the one lever for headroom: A/B-tested throughput-neutral
# (the cache is too small to matter) and frees ~0.65 GB, at a 1-2% decode
# cost. EXPERIMENTS.md section 10.
CTX=131072
NGL=all
KV_TYPE=q8_0

# --- Sampling: Ornith's values, NOT Qwen's ---
# top_k is zero, i.e. disabled. The .gguf's embedded general.sampling.* keys
# claim top_k 20 and are wrong; this is what the working deployment uses.
TEMP=1.0
TOP_P=0.95
TOP_K=0
MIN_P=0.0
REASONING_FORMAT=deepseek

# --- Throughput ---
# Not present on the running deployment, which therefore has no prompt cache:
# in an agent loop that means reprocessing the whole conversation every turn.
# EXPERIMENTS.md section 3 measured that at 35 s to first token on a 48k
# context (on the 3090). Carried over here; not re-measured on the 4090.
# Host RAM, so size it against `free -g`.
CACHE_RAM=10240

# The measured values of the running deployment. On the 4090 this pair prefills
# at 4,136-5,538 t/s with no throttling, so the 3090's prefill fix (BATCH=2048,
# UBATCH=512, EXPERIMENTS.md section 2) is NOT needed here — and, A/B-tested,
# BATCH=256 was no faster. EXPERIMENTS.md section 10.
BATCH=512
UBATCH=256

# NOT draft-mtp: this model ships NO MTP heads (scripts/gguf-info.py reports
# "MTP heads (nextn.*): 0"), so that drafter is unavailable. ngram-simple earns
# little — measured 35% acceptance over 37 drafts in 6,201 decode steps, i.e.
# 1.07 tokens per forward pass. The A/B in EXPERIMENTS.md section 10 tested
# SPEC_TYPE=none and it was NOT faster in any workload (ngram-simple was equal
# or up to ~5% ahead at longer context) — keep ngram-simple.
SPEC_TYPE=ngram-simple
SPEC_N_MAX=8
SPEC_P_MIN=0.7

# --- Exposure ---
BIND=127.0.0.1
